WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Hi, I'm Hani. Mistakes feel bad sometimes, but here's a secret: they're actually proof your brain is growing. Let's look at yours.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.833
Think of a mistake you made recently, big or small, it counts either way.

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:40.000
Think of a mistake you made recently.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.833
Notice how it felt in the moment. Embarrassed, frustrated, maybe both. That's totally normal.

00:00:45.833 --> 00:01:08.000
Notice how it felt in the moment.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.833
Here's the secret. Every mistake actually builds a tiny new bridge in your brain.

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:36.000
Here's the secret: mistakes build bridges.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.667
That bridge is your brain learning something new. A mistake is proof your brain is working.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:02:06.000
The bridge is your brain learning.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.583
So what did this mistake teach you? Even something small counts.

00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:34.000
So what did THIS mistake teach you?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:40.667
Mistakes aren't something to hide. They're something to notice, and even be a little proud of.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:03:02.000
Mistakes aren't something to hide.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:10.000
That's the Beautiful Oops. Every mistake means your brain is building something new.
